{"title":"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b11a99399c9d2053666fa2980d090149366d203.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x| + x + y = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64fac56647d2dded5cb15fddfe19ada2ed35155.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + |y| - y = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"126\" height=\"18\" />, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a859acebdd07c34704648be45c0daf108e2a29d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/7/257e47023ae8574b5977fcd6d84d2dc88769863b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -2\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{18}{5}\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{22}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"406\" height=\"37\" /> \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We proceed by casework:\n</p><p>Case 1: x, y &gt;= 0\n</p><p>Thus we have 2x + y = 10, x = 12. This makes y &lt; 0, a contradiction.\n</p><p>Case 2: x &gt;= 0 &gt; y\n</p><p>2x + y = 10, x - 2y = 12. By multiplying the first equation by two and adding, we have 4x + x = 2*10 + 12 thus x = 32/5. Since the question only specifies 1 solution, plugging in x = 32/5 into the first equation yields y = -14/5 thus x + y = 18/5 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME\" title=\"1988 AHSME\">1988 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AHSME_P